course: dictionary
lesson: 4991
title: Feelings in how people speak
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indignantly is an adverb. It tells you how someone speaks, replies or acts. Its meaning is in an angry, offended way, because you think something is unfair or insulting.
explain: «Said Alice indignantly» tells you Alice spoke crossly, but the clues around it matter. If the creatures have just been rude to her, the anger comes from feeling wronged, not just from being grumpy. Ask yourself: why would someone feel this way?
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a simpler phrase: «Alice said crossly because it was unfair» still makes sense, so you are right. Indignantly is strong, though. It means cross about something that feels unjust.
fact: Indignantly means in an angry, offended way, because you think something is unfair or insulting.
fact: Indignantly is an adverb, so it tells you how someone speaks, replies or acts.
fact: «Toad replied indignantly» means Toad answered back crossly, because he felt he had been treated unfairly.
fact: Old word meaning: indignantly = crossly, because something seems unfair.
fact: Alice often speaks indignantly in Wonderland when the creatures are rude to her.
exercise: «Toad replied indignantly.» How did Toad reply? | Quietly, so no one could hear | Happily, with a big smile | Sleepily, half asleep | *Crossly, because he felt it was unfair
exercise: «Alice spoke indignantly when the creatures were rude to her.» Why did she speak this way? | Because she had just won a prize | Because it was her birthday | *Because the creatures were rude and unfair to her | Because she was bored and sleepy
exercise: Which word means about the same as indignantly? | Barely | *Crossly | Subdued | Sadly
exercise: Maya says «indignantly» is just a fancy word for happy. What is wrong with her idea? | *It means angry and offended, not happy | It means happy and excited, so she is right | It means very quiet and shy | It means the same as tired
test: «She was blamed for something she did not do, and she protested indignantly.» What does indignantly show? | She was falling asleep | Happy surprise | *She felt the blame was unfair | She was bored
test: «"That's not fair!" she said indignantly.» What is the best meaning? | Shyly | Joyfully | *Angrily, because she thinks something is unjust | Sleepily
exam: «When the creatures called Alice rude names, she answered indignantly.» What does this tell you about how she felt? | *Hurt and cross, because it was unfair | Pleased with the creatures | Bored and tired | Afraid of the dark
